WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
Aw!

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.770
Welcome to the 20th
anniversary celebration

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.930
of Hedwig and the Angry Inch.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.317
I keep meeting people who
were affected by Hedwig.

00:00:10.317 --> 00:00:12.150
Have you heard of Hedwig
and the Angry Inch?

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.170
And I'm like, that's me.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:13.750
No way.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.490
It just doesn't stop.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.410
It's still relevant
and still beautiful.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.790
It has fostered a
conversation with strangers

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.330
about meaning and purpose.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.780
I've heard of multiple
people saying,

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.210
when I start dating someone,
if they don't like it,

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:28.500
we don't continue dating.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.972
When people come up and say
it meant something to them,

00:00:30.972 --> 00:00:32.530
it makes it more
impactful to me too.

00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:33.540
It keeps giving.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.720
It's like a personal ad that
never goes out of circulation.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:37.740
Who are you?

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:39.090
Where do you exist?

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.920
When do you get to
make that decision?

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.440
Hedwig asked that
question with music,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.520
which is the most visceral
way to ask a question.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.860
That is the most empowering
compliment any artist can have,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.780
is that it made
someone feel that they

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.480
could do something they didn't
know they could that has helped

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.030
them.

